{"raw": {"https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7b7a7621-2d08-46ed-a694-79735466f015&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201290289254_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Open Rank Professor of Counseling", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY The University of Providence seeks an accomplished academic faculty member to teach in the Master\u2019s program in Clinical Mental Health Counseling within the School of Health Professions (SHP). Reporting to the program director, the Chair will be part of the program\u2019s leadership team. Responsibilities include teaching graduate courses, evaluating program effectiveness, advising and mentoring students, developing programs and courses, and ensuring compliance with accreditation standards. Additional duties include recruiting students and representing the SHP on university-wide committees and teams. This is a remote position; however, preference will be given to candidates within commuting distance of Great Falls, MT RESPONSIBILITIES Faculty Role: Fulfill academic faculty obligations: 60% teaching, 20% scholarship, 15% service, 5% development, or as negotiated with the Dean. Recruit and advise graduate counseling students; supervise master-level interns in practicum and internship settings. Contribute to program assessment and development. Provide service to the program, the University, the profession, and the community. Develop and maintain relations with area counseling agencies, associations, and licensure boards. Leadership: Representation and Advocacy: Effectively and ethically represent the program\u2019s goals, strategies, and interests to the university internally and externally. Program Development and Improvement: Contribute to developing, reviewing, and revising the program by incorporating best practices, research, performance needs assessments, and training evaluations to maintain contemporary and relevant clinical counseling education. Program Evaluation: Participate in systematic program evaluation and assessment activities to ensure continuous quality improvement and compliance with accreditation standards (CACREP). Collaborate with other departments and stakeholders to foster interprofessional education and practice opportunities. Diversity and Inclusion: Support diversity and inclusion, fostering a positive work environment that promotes interpersonal relationships, effective communication, collaboration, and consensus building. Shared Governance: Collaborate with relevant school and university shared governance committees on matters related to academic, curricular, student, and faculty affairs. Team Collaboration: Perform all duties in a manner that promotes effective team collaboration and reflects the University and Providence\u2019s mission and philosophy. Student Experience: Ensure a positive and quality experience from recruitment and admissions through graduation. Support efforts for student recruitment, retention, and success. Address student concerns and grievances in a timely and effective manner. Policy, Accreditation, Compliance, and Quality Assurance: Participate in preparing internal and external administrative reports related to the program, including self-study and site visit preparations for accreditation. Community Engagement: Establish and maintain partnerships with healthcare organizations to provide quality clinical experiences for students. Represent the program at professional conferences and community events. Professional Development: Maintain current knowledge of higher education, health professions, and clinical counseling by attending state and national conferences and participating in other professional development activities to ensure the university\u2019s programs remain robust, current, and relevant. \u00a0 QUALIFICATIONS EDUCATION: PhD in Counselor Education from a CACREP accredited program (required). Certified Rehabilitation Counselor (CRC) (preferred).\u00a0 Licensed Addiction Counselor (LAC) (preferred). EXPERIENCE: Teaching experience in higher education, with a preference for experience in teaching graduate-level courses. Demonstrated success in curriculum development, program evaluation, and accreditation. Experience with distance education and online learning platforms. Proven ability in academic networking and commitment to integrating best practices into academic systems and processes. Evidence of ongoing scholarly activity. LICENSURE If eligible for professional licensure (e.g., Professional Counselor, National Certified Counselor, Certified Rehabilitation Counselor), must hold a current, unencumbered license and be eligible for licensure in the State of Montana. The University of Providence is an equal opportunity employer covered by the Montana veterans\u2019 and handicapped persons\u2019 employment preference act. The University of Providence is a Catholic, student-centered, mission-focused university. For more information, please contact Human Resources at 406.791.5977.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7b7a7621-2d08-46ed-a694-79735466f015&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201278685119_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Biology", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-31\n\nLocation: Great Falls\n\nPOSITION SUMMARY The University of Providence invites applications for an Adjunct Instructor of Biology \u00a0at our campus in \u00a0Great Falls, Montana to teach undergraduate biology courses as assigned. Teaching opportunities may include Anatomy & Physiology, Microbiology, General Biology, and other courses aligned with the candidate's academic preparation and expertise. Candidates with experience and/or expertise in Forensic Science or Chemistry are encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to student success and excellence in teaching while supporting the University's mission as a Catholic, student-centered, mission-focused institution. RESPONSIBILITIES Teach assigned undergraduate Biology courses in accordance with departmental and University standards. Prepare and deliver course materials, lectures, laboratory activities, and assessments. Maintain accurate student records and submit grades according to established University policies and deadlines. Hold reasonable office hours or be available to students by appointment. Foster an engaging, inclusive, and supportive learning environment. Communicate regularly with department leadership regarding course needs and student success. Adhere to University policies, procedures, and academic standards. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Education Master's degree in Biology or a closely related field required. Doctorate in Biology or a related discipline preferred. Experience Demonstrated success teaching college-level Biology courses or relevant professional experience in the biological sciences. Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work effectively with a diverse population of students, faculty, and staff. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience teaching Anatomy & Physiology and/or Microbiology. Experience teaching in online or hybrid learning environments. Expertise in Forensic Science. Familiarity with learning management systems and instructional technology. POSITION DETAILS Position Type: Adjunct Faculty FLSA Status: Exempt Location: Great Falls, Montana Appointment: Part-time, contingent upon enrollment and departmental needs Compensation: Adjunct faculty are compensated on a per-credit basis ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY OF PROVIDENCE The University of Providence is a Catholic, student-centered, mission-focused university committed to academic excellence, service, and the development of the whole person. EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY The University of Providence is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal and state employment laws, including the Montana Veterans' and Handicapped Persons' Employment Preference Act.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7b7a7621-2d08-46ed-a694-79735466f015&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201270766488_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Custodian", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-02\n\nLocation: Great Falls\n\nJoin a Mission-Driven Team Where Your Work Matters The University of Providence is seeking a dedicated Custodian to help create a clean, safe, welcoming environment for our students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Whether you are starting your career or looking for a stable position with exceptional benefits, we invite you to become part of a community grounded in dignity, compassion, excellence, integrity, and service. [uprovidence.edu] , [uprovidence.edu] At UP, custodians are essential members of our campus community. The work you do every day directly supports student success and helps create an environment where learning and personal growth can flourish. Why Work at the University of Providence? Outstanding Benefits Package We believe great employees deserve great benefits. Benefit-eligible employees enjoy access to: \u2705 Comprehensive Medical, Dental, and Vision Coverage with multiple plan options available. \u2705 University-Paid Benefits , including: Basic Life Insurance Short-Term Disability Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Caregiver Assistance Program and well-being resources \u2705 Retirement Savings Through TIAA University contribution of 4% of salary after one year of service Immediate eligibility for employee contributions through payroll deduction \u2705 Generous Paid Time Off Vacation leave Personal holidays Additional paid holidays and leave benefits as applicable \u2705 Additional Voluntary Benefits Flexible Spending Accounts Supplemental Life Insurance Accident and Critical Illness Insurance Identity and Credit Protection Legal Coverage Options More Than a Job The University of Providence is a mission-focused Catholic university with a strong sense of community and service. Employees enjoy meaningful work, supportive colleagues, and the opportunity to contribute to an institution that changes lives through education. Position Summary The Custodian is responsible for maintaining the cleanliness, sanitation, and appearance of assigned campus facilities. This position performs a variety of custodial duties to ensure a safe and welcoming environment for the entire University community. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Sweep, mop, scrub, strip, wax, and buff floors, hallways, and stairways. Vacuum and shampoo carpets and rugs. Dust and clean furniture, walls, ceilings, windows, and other building surfaces. Clean, sanitize, and restock restrooms and other common areas. Collect and dispose of trash and transport recyclable materials. Move furniture as needed for cleaning and event support. Observe and follow all safety and security procedures. Identify and report maintenance concerns. Perform special cleaning projects and other duties as assigned. Note: Work schedules may vary and can include swing shift, graveyard shift, weekends, and holidays. Qualifications Required Valid Montana Driver's License. Ability to follow oral and written instructions. Ability to read and understand chemical labels and safety information. Ability to perform basic math for measuring and mixing cleaning solutions. Ability to safely operate cleaning equipment, including vacuums, floor buffers, and floor waxers. Ability to perform physical work involving standing, bending, lifting, and operating equipment. Experience and Education No previous custodial experience is required. No minimum education requirement applies. We are willing to train dependable individuals who take pride in their work. What We're Looking For Successful candidates will demonstrate: Dependability and strong work ethic Commitment to customer service Integrity and professionalism Teamwork and collaboration Respect for diverse individuals and perspectives Commitment to maintaining a safe and welcoming campus environment Apply Today If you're looking for a stable position with excellent benefits, a supportive team, and an opportunity to make a difference every day, we encourage you to apply for the Custodian position at the University of Providence. Build your future while helping create an exceptional campus experience for our students and community.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7b7a7621-2d08-46ed-a694-79735466f015&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201267333288_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Nursing Adjunct Instructor", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-22\n\nLocation: Great Falls\n\nAdjunct Nursing Faculty POSITION SUMMARY University of Providence is seeking a dedicated and experienced Adjunct Nursing Faculty to join our institution's nursing program. Adjunct Nursing Faculty have a vital role in providing quality education to nursing students, contributing to their academic and professional development. This position involves teaching nursing courses, facilitating clinical experiences, and participating in curriculum development to ensure the delivery of an exceptional nursing program. Adjunct Faculty are not eligible for tenure. Adjunct positions are located either on or off-campus with the option for remote work. Position will entail both clinical and didactic responsibilities. Experience in maternal-child nursing, pediatric nursing, behavioral health nursing preferred. Additional nursing expertise will be considered.\u00a0 RESPONSIBILITIES Adjunct Faculty: Carries a teaching load of no more than 14 credit hours per academic year Course teaching includes the full-range BSN nursing content in both didactic and clinical teaching depending on expertise: nursing leadership, clinical nursing practice, evidence-based practice, physiology and pharmacology, and community and population health; all courses reflect baccalaureate education standards (AACN Essentials for Baccalaureate Education for Professional Nursing Practice, 2021) Assists with academic and quality processes to maintain full Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (CCNE) Accreditation for the nursing program. May conduct or work with a team to conduct and publish research projects as a mechanism in developing the nursing program, faculty and students. Research findings and research projects will be conducted in collaboration with the Providence System Office Research Council.\u00a0 Provides service to the program, university, profession, and community.\u00a0 Engages in scholarly activities to include academic publications and research presentations at national conferences to further advance the nursing profession.\u00a0 May assist with program management, accreditation, curricula, and quality improvement. The faculty position is located on campus and faculty are required to attend faculty development and other required events indicated by the nursing program and/or university. Travel is paid for by the nursing program. Position may include both clinical and didactic responsibilities. \u00a0 REQUIREMENTS EDUCATION MSN Graduate degree in nursing required; Earned doctorate in nursing or higher education-related field preferred. Current, unencumbered RN license in the state of current residence. Ability to obtain a Montana state RN License (or privilege to practice from the Nurse Licensure Compact).\u00a0 EXPERIENCE Knowledge and understanding of adult learning and educational theories and techniques. Proficient computer skills and a working knowledge of software programs and communication methods is required; this includes Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, & PowerPoint). Excellent written and oral communications skills\u00a0 Ability to work independently, with minimal supervision and excellent time management skills. POSITION DETAILS Position Type:\u00a0 Contract-Term\u00a0 FTE: 0.25 FLSA:\u00a0 Exempt Salary: $1070/credit Location: Great Falls, Montana \u00a0 AN AFFIRMATIVE ACTION/EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER COVERED BY THE MONTANA VETERANS\u2019 AND HANDICAPPED PERSONS\u2019 EMPLOYMENT PREFERENCE ACT The University of Providence is a Catholic, student-centered, mission-focused university. For more information, please contact Human Resources at 406.791.5976", "department": ""}}, "rows": {"https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7b7a7621-2d08-46ed-a694-79735466f015&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201290289254_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 763, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7b7a7621-2d08-46ed-a694-79735466f015&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201290289254_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Open Rank Professor of Counseling", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor; Full_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "School of Health Professions", "area_key_words": "Counseling", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-09-08", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7b7a7621-2d08-46ed-a694-79735466f015&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201278685119_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 763, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7b7a7621-2d08-46ed-a694-79735466f015&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201278685119_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Adjunct Instructor of Biology", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Biology; hybrid learning environments", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-07-31", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7b7a7621-2d08-46ed-a694-79735466f015&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201270766488_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 763, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7b7a7621-2d08-46ed-a694-79735466f015&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201270766488_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Custodian", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-07-02", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7b7a7621-2d08-46ed-a694-79735466f015&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201267333288_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 763, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7b7a7621-2d08-46ed-a694-79735466f015&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201267333288_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Nursing Adjunct Instructor", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Nursing Adjunct", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-06-22", "position_start_date": ""}}, "school_id": 763, "status": "complete", "updated_at": "2026-10-27T00:42:44+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-10-27T00:42:44+00:00", "last_error": ""}